From: CI Fix <ci-fix@example.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 20:11:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CI: hermetic OPENAI_API_KEY in tests + align
 safety-language wording

- tests/conftest.py: lock OPENAI_API_KEY to "" at collection time so
  load_dotenv() in backend/app.py can never pull a real key from a
  committed/local .env into the test session (python-dotenv's
  load_dotenv() defaults to override=False, so setting the var first
  wins). Fixes test_chat.py::test_chat_start_returns_session_id, which
  expects chatbot_mode == "error" with no key configured. Does not
  touch any real .env file.

- src/chatbot/llm_client.py: reworded _build_system_prompt() so the
  three required safety phrases ("do not diagnose", "safety analysis
  result provided by the analyzer", "encourage human support") are
  present verbatim and in context, matching
  test_llm_client.py::test_system_prompt_matches_required_safety_language.
  Semantic content is unchanged -- this is a wording alignment, not a
  new claim. Also applied black formatting to the touched block.
